      "content": "It's clear that your love for your family motivates you to make such serious and compassionate decisions. However, it's important to challenge the idea of seeing yourself only as the \"end of the line.\" Everyone's life has deeper worth and potential, including yours. While genetic and systemic issues do play a role in the struggles you've mentioned, they don't dictate the entire narrative of your family's future. With the right support, interventions, and healing strategies, it's possible for families to break from these cycles. Your own path doesn't have to end in despair. There's profound strength in your willingness to seek ways to improve, not just your life, but the lives of your loved ones. Remember, the most beautiful beginnings often come from overcoming seemingly insurmountable obstacles, and your journey might just inspire more positive change than you imagine.",
      "source": "target",
